<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Light showers seen over parts of S.Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Light showers seen over parts of S.Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department forecast light showers in the Central, Sabaragamuwa and Western provinces and over Galle and Matara districts for Thursday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement on Wednesday that gusts of fairly strong westerly winds will continue to prevail along the western slopes of the central hills and elsewhere during showers.</p>
<p>It released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Wednesday morning:</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Canyon		   8.5</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	    8.7</p>
<p>    Kotmale		   0</p>
<p>    Laxapana		 7.0</p>
<p>    Moussakele	     4.0</p>
<p>    Norton		   7.7</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	    0</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   0</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  0</p>
</text>
